* {{l|en|bonie}} {{qualifier|obsolete}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|en|enm|*bonie}} (attested only rarely as {{m|enm|bon}}, {{m|enm|boun}}), probably from {{der|en|fro|bon}}, feminine {{m|fro|bonne||[[good]]}}, from {{der|en|la|bonus||good}}. See {{m|en|bounty}}, and compare {{m|en|bonus}}, {{m|en|boon}}.

====Adjective====
{{en-adj|er|more}}

# [[merry|Merry]]; [[happy]].
#: {{syn|en|frolicsome|cheerful|blithe|gay}}
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Much Ado About Nothing|text=''Be you blithe and '''bonny'''''<br>Converting all your sounds of woe<br>Into Hey nonny, nonny.}}
# {{lb|en|Scotland|Geordie}} [[beautiful|Beautiful]]; [[pretty]]; [[attractive]]; [[handsome]].
#* {{quote-song|en|lyricist=w:Robert Burns|title=w:Handsome Nell|year=1774|year_published=1803|passage=O once I lov'd a '''bonnie''' lass, / Aye, and I love her still}}
# {{lb|en|Scotland|Geordie}} [[fine|Fine]], [[good]] (often used ironically).
#: {{ux|en|My '''bonnie''' friend, come over here.}}

